## What is wrong

`on_finish` computes `$exit_code = $status >> 8` (`lib/Net/Async/MCP/Run.pm:225`) and ignores the low byte of the wait status. When the process the shell exec'd dies from a signal (SIGKILL from the OOM killer, SIGSEGV, SIGPIPE), `$status >> 8` is 0, and `_format_result` (`Run.pm:288`) derives `isError` from that.

## Reproduce

    tools/call run { command => 'kill -9 $$' }
    # {"content":[{"text":"Exit code: 0\n\n=== STDOUT ===\n"}],"isError":0}

The model is told a crashed command succeeded.

## Done

- A signal death maps to the shell convention `128 + signal` (or is reported as its own `=== ERROR === killed by signal N` section) and sets `isError`.
- Test with `kill -9 $$` and `kill -TERM $$`.

